# Embedded Firmware (Complement)

When working with embedded C, firmware, or hardware-adjacent code, also consult the **abase-embedded-systems** skill for structured guidance. This rule complements it with patterns from jeffallan/embedded-systems.

- Prefer deterministic behavior; avoid reliance on timing assumptions where possible.
- Document hardware dependencies and pin mappings in code comments or a hardware doc.
- Use defensive checks (null, bounds) even when "it should never happen" in embedded contexts.
